  "goodToKnow": "Der Verleger (die Verlegerin) is a publisher, the person who owns or runs a publishing house, der Verlag. Germany has a strong publishing tradition: the Frankfurter Buchmesse is the world's largest book fair, and Leipzig was the historic centre of the book trade. Verlegen means to publish, but also to move or postpone and to mislay: Ich habe meine Brille verlegt. Verlegen as an adjective means embarrassed."
